    </ul>

    <h3>Deepavali (Kali Puja)</h3>
    <figure class="figure--float">
      <img src="{{ '/assets/images/ashram1.webp' | url }}" alt="Ananda Ashram Kali Puja">
    </figure>
    <p>This special worship of the Shyam-Shyama deity was conceived and planned by Sri Thakur himself. In this unique form, the Mother Kali holds a Asii (sword) and a Banshi (flute) in one hand and a Shankha (conch) and a Chakra (discus) in the other two hands. Her crown is adorned with Shikhi Pakha (peacock feathers).</p>
    <p>On the morning after the Shyam–Shyama Puja, the Andul Kali Kirtan Samity offers devotional songs in praise of the Divine Mother. These songs are more than 150 years old, traditionally scripted by a spiritual personality Sri Premik Maharaj residing at Andul, a small village in Howrah, West Bengal. The above occasions are celebrated through worship, Naam Sankirtan, offerings of bhog-rag and distribution of prasadam to the disciples and devotees.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Kailash Centres &amp; Activities</h2>
    <p>Swami Shivananda Giri Maharaj founded Kailash in the year 1978, as an attempt to spread welfare activities across our society. He named the organization after the untimely death of one of his closest disciples, Kailash Ghosh, who was then a reputed football player, playing for a first division club of Kolkata. <!-- TODO confirm with client: does the football-player detail refer to Kailash Ghosh, or to Maharaj? --> Maharaj imbued his followers and disciples with the spirit and ideals of selfless service, inspiring them to stand beside those in distress and to serve humanity with compassion and dedication. Apart from being an encyclopaedia on religion, Maharaj wrote and composed prose and songs and His kirtans were widely popular across continents.</p>
    <p>Kailash is a non-profit organization founded by most revered Swami Shivananda Giri Maharaj with the primary motto of helping people in need. As a philanthropic organization, Kailash has been working for over 48 years. At the Registered office 21/2 Beadon Street, Kolkata, all the official works are conducted here, along with the following activities:</p>
    <h3>Following Activities</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Dr. S K Gupta Memorial Charitable Clinic — Free Eye Clinic for Eye checking with spectacles, Free Homeopathy Clinic for health check up with medicines</li>
      <!-- TODO confirm with client: "Panch Sike Panch Ana" here vs. "Panch Sike Panch Aana" on the Publications page — pick one spelling. -->
      <li>Publication Unit — publish Panch Sike Panch Ana the monthly magazine and books on Maharaj</li>
      <li>Anandam Granthagar — a beautifully arranged library, curated by Maharaj</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Kailash Runs Other Two Centres</h2>

    <h3>Vivekananda Snehanir</h3>
    <figure>
      <img src="{{ '/assets/images/vivekananda.webp' | url }}" alt="Vivekananda Snehanir">
    </figure>
    <p>Vivekananda Snehanir (the foster care unit for boys at Somrabazar, Hooghly) is a home for under-privileged children (not orphans).</p>
    <p>Vivekananda Snehanir was Kailash&rsquo;s first social-work initiative, founded in 1979. The old building was a rented house in the village of Somrabazar. A new self-owned Home was built in the year 2019 in the same village relocating our children. The new space is a two-storied building with senior and junior boys' wards in the ground floor with dining space, kitchen, computer lab and office. The 1st floor houses a prayer and meeting hall with two guest rooms. Vivekananda Snehanir is a Home to 18 boys at present where Kailash bears all expenses of their accommodation, food, education and essentials. The boys attend the local Govt. aided school. They also get guidance and in house educational coaching, computer training, Yoga training. This centre is powered by Solar Systems.</p>

    <h4>Social Activities</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Free Eye Clinic for Eye checking with spectacles</li>
      <li>Free Homeopathy Clinic for health check up with medicines</li>
      <li>Distribution of blankets, clothing, and food to underprivileged and needy people of the adjoining places</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>Annual Festivals &amp; Ceremonies</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Maharaj's Abirvab Tithi Puja Utsav — celebrated on Akshya Tritiya each year with Puja, Naam Sankirtan, offerings of bhog-rag and distribution of prasadam attended by the devotees, parents of the boys, ex-students with their families and also by the friends of Kailash from different social working groups</li>
      <li>Saraswati Puja</li>
      <li>Independence Day</li>
      <li>Teacher's Day</li>
      <li>Yoga &amp; Sports Day</li>
      <li>Birthday Celebration of each boy with fun and food</li>
    </ul>

